	(text "MCU — STM32G0B1CBT6, LQFP-48\n\nPOWER\n- VDD and VBAT: 3.3 V; VSS: GND.\n- C12/C13: 4.7 uF + 100 nF supply decoupling.\n  Place close to VDD/VSS.\n- VREF+: 3.3 V ADC reference.\n- C10/C11: 1 uF + 100 nF reference decoupling.\n  Keep VREFBUF disabled and in high-impedance mode.\n- VBAT tied to VDD; no independent battery backup.\n\nRESET\n- NRST: Active-low reset.\n- R2: 10 kohm external pull-up.\n- SW1: Press to pull NRST low and reset the MCU.\n- C5: 100 nF reset filtering.\n\nCLOCKS\n- X2: 8 MHz HSE crystal; C8/C9: 20 pF.\n- X1: 32.768 kHz LSE crystal; C6/C7: 10 pF.\n- Load capacitor values must match the selected crystals.\n- Place crystals and capacitors close to MCU clock pins.\n  Keep traces short and away from switching signals.\n\nINTERFACES\n- PD0/PD1: FDCAN1 RX/TX.\n- PA2/PA3: USART2 TX/RX.\n- PA4–PA7: SPI1 CS/SCK/MISO/MOSI.\n- PB10/PB11: I2C2 SCL/SDA; external pull-ups required.\n  Pull-ups may be provided by the connected module.\n- PB0/PB1: TIM3 CH3/CH4 PWM.\n- PA0/PA1: ADC inputs.\n- PA13/PA14: SWDIO/SWCLK; reserve for debugging.\n- KEY_ROW1–4 / KEY_COL1–3: 4x3 matrix keypad.\n\nTEST POINTS\n- TP2: 3.3 V.\n- TP3: GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.526 156.464 0)
		(effects
